  <link href="https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/draft-ietf-ospf-two-part-metric-10" rel="prev"/>
<link href="https://dx.doi.org/10.17487/rfc8042" rel="alternate"/>
  <front>
    <title>OSPF Two-Part Metric</title>
    <seriesInfo name="RFC" value="8042" stream="IETF"/>
    <date year="2016" month="December"/>
    <abstract pn="section-abstract">
      <t indent="0" pn="section-abstract-1">This document specifies an optional OSPF protocol extension to
represent router metrics in a multi-access network in two parts: the
metric from the router to the network and the metric from the network
to the router.  For such networks, the router-to-router metric for
OSPF route computation is the sum of the two parts.  This document
updates RFC 2328.</t>
    </abstract>
